      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Working: Ternary Operator"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This is our code from earlier example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "1#include <iostream>\n2using namespace std;\n3\n4int main() {\n5\n6    int marks = 76;\n7\n8    string result = (marks >= 32) ? \"pass\" : \"fail\";\n9  \n10    cout << result;\n11\n12    return 0;\n13}\n14\n15// Output:\n16// pass"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Notice the code,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "string result = (marks >= 32) ? \"pass\" : \"fail\";"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, (marks >= 32) is a test expression that results in either true or false. If the test expression is"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "true - \"pass\" (string before the colon :) is assigned to the result variable",
        "false - \"fail\" (string after the colon :) is assigned to the result variable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "From the example, we can deduce the syntax of ternary operator as:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "(test_condition) ? expression1 : expression2;"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "The ternary operator executes the part before the : symbol if test_expresion is true, else it executes the part after the: symbol",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, when the test_condition is true, expression1 is executed and when the test condition is false, expression2 is executed."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "You can see there are 3 operands here, hence the name ternary operator."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
